lessons_learned.solution:
The executeCommand function in EPaxos blocks indefinitely waiting for dependencies to become COMMITTED (via a sleep loop in strongconnect). When testing execution with unready dependencies, run executeCommand in a goroutine and use a timeout channel to detect blocking behavior. This is the correct protocol behavior - execution should wait for dependencies. Example:
```go
executionDone := make(chan bool, 1)
go func() {
    result := replica.exec.executeCommand(r, i)
    executionDone <- result
}()
select {
case result := <-executionDone:
    // Execution completed
case <-time.After(2 * time.Second):
    // Execution is blocking (expected for unready dependencies)
}
```
